  "notes": "Represents the 'IT field' request \u2014 the general 'Information Sciences and Technology, B.S.' major (ISSWC_BS) was tried first but turned out to have no University Park Suggested Academic Plan (effectively World-Campus-only / not currently offered at any campus), so this major was substituted: it has a real, current, University Park-based 4-year plan. 'Application Focus Selection' slots (9 credits across 3 terms) are chosen from a College-approved list not enumerated in the bulletin's course table. 'etm' marks the courses everything else in the sequence assumes are done. For 2022-23 through 2024-25, the courses now cross-listed as CYBER 221/451/454/456 only existed as SRA 221/IST 451/IST 454/IST 456 (no CYBER-prefix alternative yet). UPDATE after the prereq-parser fix: both STAT 200 and its SCM 200 alternate require MATH 21 (which needs MATH 4, which needs MATH 3), none of which were anywhere in this plan -- added the MATH 3 -> MATH 4 -> MATH 21 chain explicitly (front of Semesters 1-3), same fix as the 2026 plan. Also dropped the generic, unenumerated 3cr 'Elective' slot (Semester 8) to partially offset the 9 new credits. FLAGGED FOR HUMAN REVIEW (same as 2026): even after that offset, this plan cannot be packed into exactly 8 real terms under the simulator's greedy scheduler -- a real consequence of the newly-correct STAT 200 prereq chain, not a data error. RESOLVED (was flagged for human review): CYBER 342W's real prereq_groups requires the literal course code CYBER 221, but this plan (matching this catalog year's real historical bulletin) only offered SRA 221, which no longer exists as a standalone catalog entry post-rename. Since SRA 221/IST 451/454/456 are the exact same courses as their now-current CYBER-prefixed cross-listings (just renamed, not different content), added CYBER 221/451/454/456 as alternate options alongside the original historical codes -- same modeling convention the 2026 plan already uses for its own cross-listings -- which lets the plan resolve through real, currently-cataloged course data. Also removed MATH 3/MATH 4 (now-unnecessary padding, see 2026 plan's notes for why). HANDBOOK VERIFICATION PASS (real archived bulletin, bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2023-2024/.../cybersecurity-analytics-operations-bs/): wired all 3 'Application Focus Selection' slots with a 'match' regex built from this catalog year's real 6-track list (adds Enterprise Technology vs. 2022's list; Application Development drops IST 110; Law and Policy and Geopolitics gain several new codes). Same convention/caveats as the 2022 fix above.",
